==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*slouβrikos}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*slewbʰ-||slip, slide}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|lūbricus}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj|lūbricus}}

# [[slippery]], [[slimy]]
# [[fleeting]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|5|475-476|quote=mandantem amplectī cupiunt et bracchia tendunt:<br/>'''lūbrica''' prēnsantēs effugit umbra manūs|trans=''[As he is] entrusting [his request to them], they long to embrace [him] and extend their arms: the '''fleeting''' shade eludes their grasping hands.''<br/>(The ghost of Remus appears to his foster-parents {{w|Faustulus}} and {{w|Acca Larentia}}; see also {{w|Romulus and Remus}}.)}}
# [[inconstant]]
# [[deceitful]]
#* '''4th-century CE''', Jerome of Stridon (St. Jerome), ''Vulgate'', 26:28
#*: Lingua fallāx nōn amat vēritātem et os '''lūbricum''' operātur ruīnās.
#*:: ''A deceitful tongue loveth not truth: and a '''slippery''' mouth worketh ruin.''
#*::: (trans.: Douay-Rheims Bible)
# [[hazardous]], [[unsteady]]
# [[tricky]]

